{"title":"2026 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 13","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4(Quick_And_Easy)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4(Quick And Easy)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Solution_6_(Without_Pythagoras_or_Distance_Formula)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 6 (Without Pythagoras or Distance Formula)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Daily_Dose_of_Math\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Daily Dose of Math</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_DDM\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by DDM</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Thinking_Feet\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Thinking Feet</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_SpreadTheMathLove\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">11</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by SpreadTheMathLove</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-12\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_SquishBJ_(AIME_Qualifier)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">12</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by SquishBJ (AIME Qualifier)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-13\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_in_Chinese_by_SquishBJ_(AIME_Qualifier)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">13</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution in Chinese by SquishBJ (AIME Qualifier)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-14\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">14</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The figure below shows a tiling of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/9/3b931b4ecb324b5389d91919ee30d53b913cd5b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 \\times 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"39\" height=\"12\" /> unit squares. Each row of unit squares is shifted horizontally by half a unit relative to the row above it. A shaded square is drawn on top of the tiling. Each vertex of the shaded square is a vertex of one of the unit squares. In square units, what is the area of the shaded square?\n</p><p><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:2026_amc_8_q13.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/3/36/2026_amc_8_q13.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"650\" height=\"542\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/1/891d647dc4cc52fc070643b6c42f3aa5e39de404.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\textbf{A. } 10 \\quad \\textbf{B. }  \\frac{21}{2}  \\quad \\textbf{C. }  \\frac{32}{3}  \\quad \\textbf{D. } 11 \\quad \\textbf{E. } \\frac{34}{3}\\]\" width=\"294\" height=\"37\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Label the vertices <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, in clockwise order. Then, we use coordinate geometry to easily solve this. Let point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> be on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/b/c4b86f54134d69cad8793688a431aa907aaf2698.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0, 0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"42\" height=\"20\" />. Then, point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> is 1 unit up and 3 right of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/b/c4b86f54134d69cad8793688a431aa907aaf2698.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0, 0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"42\" height=\"20\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/6/d261236ea904095d8d185a456444545b5206013b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(3, 1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />. The figure is said to be a square. and so we just calculate the distance from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/b/c4b86f54134d69cad8793688a431aa907aaf2698.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0, 0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"42\" height=\"20\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/4/c04c2d1bd65c882efed8513bbbf77022aba66364.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(3,1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />. Using the distance formula, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/5/f8519cd0f3e70c6c1208fa7944bf99574c4f14b8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{(1-0)^2 + (3-0)^2} = \\sqrt{(1+9)} = \\sqrt{10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"320\" height=\"35\" />. The area is just this value squared, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/7/cd7ae6c302dec5c5be789f3d4d9be37d000d0772.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"30\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p><p>~Pinotation\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since the side length of a square is 1 unit, we can use Pythagoras on a side length (note that we only need to find one side since the shape is a square). If we do it on the left side, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/e/72e2b4fcf1050eb8a4a7a765ea484c977a0376c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{3^2+(0.5+0.5)^2}=\\sqrt{10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"206\" height=\"35\" />. Therefore, the final area is the side length squared, which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/2/d7205980b278b681f6457dbc719649b4e373f7ef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(\\sqrt{10})^2=\\boxed{\\textbf{(A) }10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"146\" height=\"30\" />. ~Baihly2024\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Notice that the top-left side of our square is the hypotenuse of a right triangle with legs of length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />cm and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />cm. Using the Pythagorean Theorem, the side length of our square is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/6/fd66fa961a04bb1fc32d7ac40105d5d3f41fc9d6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{1^2+3^2}=\\sqrt{10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"130\" height=\"21\" />cm, so the area is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/3/be3885da65d04a14a48d9a655ca6424aff7a623d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{10}^2=10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"85\" height=\"24\" />cm<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/0/2f095616666d4fcaba292be9fb5b5e79e96da54c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: 7px\" width=\"6\" height=\"7\" />, so we obtain <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/c/bccc2b978789bdae3357ddd8481ef68495b3f0b1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(A) }10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"65\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p><p>~Yuhao2012\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_4.28Quick_And_Easy.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4(Quick_And_Easy)\">Solution 4(Quick And Easy)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4(Quick And Easy)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Notice that we can construct a 4x4 square that passes tangent to each corner. The area of this square is 16. This square forms 4 congruent right triangles, with a base of 3 and height of 1. The area of one of these triangles is 1.5, and you can multiply that by 4 to get the total area of these triangles, 6. Subtract that from the area of the constructed square to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/c/bccc2b978789bdae3357ddd8481ef68495b3f0b1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(A) }10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"65\" height=\"28\" />. as your answer.\n</p><p>It would look something like  <span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:2026_amc_8_q13_ans.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/a/aa/2026_amc_8_q13_ans.png/650px-2026_amc_8_q13_ans.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"650\" height=\"529\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/a/aa/2026_amc_8_q13_ans.png/975px-2026_amc_8_q13_ans.png 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/a/aa/2026_amc_8_q13_ans.png/1300px-2026_amc_8_q13_ans.png 2x\" /></a></span>\n</p><p>~ AskNamanYT\n</p><p>image by -N.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5\">Solution 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Similar to Solution 4, we construct one right triangle outside the square. We can see that it has side lengths 3 and 1. Using the Pythagorean Theorem we find that the hypotenuse, which is also a side of the original square, is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/4/1c4f56670a613c679c0291375283e37df33f3a78.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"33\" height=\"18\" />. Now, we can find the area of the square by squaring that, which yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/c/bccc2b978789bdae3357ddd8481ef68495b3f0b1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(A) }10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"65\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p><p>~Lightning_Fox\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_6_.28Without_Pythagoras_or_Distance_Formula.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_6_(Without_Pythagoras_or_Distance_Formula)\">Solution 6 (Without Pythagoras or Distance Formula)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 6 (Without Pythagoras or Distance Formula)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li>Note: this solution is unreliable and only use it if you have no other methods to solve.</li></ul>\n<p>We can count the number of small squares inside the large square and add <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to our running count if the square is more than half shaded, add <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/9/2f960094315d60883495f9b74148e17487ee9584.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> if it is exactly (or almost exactly) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/9/2f960094315d60883495f9b74148e17487ee9584.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> shaded, and add <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> if it is less than half shaded. Counting the squares, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> fully shaded, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> more than half, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> exactly half. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/9/60994a363c8fa4921ac51481518f5c3bf57f4b9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5+4+2\\times{\\frac{1}{2}}=\\boxed{\\textbf{(A)} 10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"192\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>~jeremyq\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Daily_Dose_of_Math\">Video Solution by Daily Dose of Math</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Daily Dose of Math\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/gzXlOkLl24U\">https://youtu.be/gzXlOkLl24U</a>\n</p><p>~TheSmartGreekMathDude\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_DDM\">Video Solution by DDM</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by DDM\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/nY1hhVbEeBk\">https://youtu.be/nY1hhVbEeBk</a>\n</p><p>~piggydude\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Thinking_Feet\">Video Solution by Thinking Feet</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Thinking Feet\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/xSsKQiHLBfU\">https://youtu.be/xSsKQiHLBfU</a>\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_SpreadTheMathLove\">Video Solution by SpreadTheMathLove</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by SpreadTheMathLove\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=YJnsl4zjdK8\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=YJnsl4zjdK8</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_by_SquishBJ_.28AIME_Qualifier.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_SquishBJ_(AIME_Qualifier)\">Video Solution by SquishBJ (AIME Qualifier)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=12\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by SquishBJ (AIME Qualifier)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3GmtxMC-W1I&amp;t=1305s\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3GmtxMC-W1I&amp;t=1305s</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_in_Chinese_by_SquishBJ_.28AIME_Qualifier.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_in_Chinese_by_SquishBJ_(AIME_Qualifier)\">Video Solution in Chinese by SquishBJ (AIME Qualifier)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=13\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution in Chinese by SquishBJ (AIME Qualifier)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.bilibili.com/video/BV18GME64EYA/\">https://www.bilibili.com/video/BV18GME64EYA/</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=14\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a h